## Summary

Done. Both the implementation and the tests are in place and verified.

**`Sources/NoteKit/NoteKit.swift`** (added after the existing `Note` struct):
- `public enum NoteParseError: Error, Equatable { case malformedFormat }`
- `public func parseNote(from text: String) throws -> Note` — splits on the **literal** separator `\n---\n` (the 7-char string backslash-n-dash-dash-dash-backslash-n, written in Swift as `"\\n---\\n"`), then:
  - throws `NoteParseError.malformedFormat` unless `text` splits into exactly 4 fields (using `omittingEmptySubsequences: false`, so an empty id counts as a field rather than being silently dropped);
  - maps fields 0–3 → `id`, `title`, `pinned` flag, `body`;
  - derives `tags` by reusing the existing `extractTags(from:)` (no reimplementation);
  - `pinned` is `true` only when the flag field equals `"1"`.

**`Tests/NoteKitTests/NoteKitTests.swift`** (added 4 tests): round-trip, `pinned=false` for flag `"0"`, empty-id allowed, and malformedFormat thrown for 1/3/5 fields.

